  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria Country Operational Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">14 million Syrians require some form of income and livelihoods support</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Syria Country Operational Plan
MAASY002</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Meeting basic needs through cash and voucher assistance.
Increasing the proportion of assistance that is delivered through cash and voucher assistance including livelihoods and food security interventions where feasible, based on market assessments
Prepositioning and distributing food and non-food relief items to 10,000 households
Distributing agriculture related inputs (seeds, pesticides, fertilizers, livestock), and/or grants for food security, food production and agriculture restoration to 16,000 households</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Syrian crisis today is more critical than ever. Nearly 15 million people are in need of humanitarian assistance, including 12 million facing acute food insecurity. It was estimated that 14 million Syrians would require some form of income and livelihoods support in 2022, a staggering increase from 10 million in 2020.</narrative>
  </description>
